pedia/commons/3/3c/Metropolitan_New_York_Library_Council_twitter_logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Saints Kyril & Metodi Bulgarian Eastern Orthodox Diocesan Cathedral","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":40.765461,"lo":-73.994182,"d":408,"ds":"Saints Kyril & Metodi Bulgarian Eastern Orthodox Diocesan Cathedral (sometimes SS. Kiril and Methodi) is the cathedral church and headquarters of the Bulgarian Orthodox Church Diocese of the United States, Canada, and Australia. The church is located at 552 West 50th Street, between Tenth and Eleventh Avenues, Hell's Kitchen / Clinton, Manhattan, New York City.","wpu":"Saints Kyril & Metodi Bulgarian Eastern Orthodox Diocesan Cathedral","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Saints_Kyril_%26_Metodi_Bulgarian_Eastern_Orthodox_Cathedral_01.JPG/960px-Saints_Kyril_%26_Metodi_Bulgarian_Eastern_Orthodox_Cathedral_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"DeWitt Clinton Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":40.768211,"lo":-73.994303,"d":532,"ds":"DeWitt Clinton Park is a 5.8-acre (23,000 m2) New York City public park in the Hell's Kitchen neighborhood of Manhattan, New York City, between West 52nd and 54th Streets, and Eleventh and Twelfth Avenues.","wpu":"DeWitt Clinton Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Clinton-park1.jpg/960px-Clinton-park1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ensemble Studio Theatre","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":40.766953,"lo":-73.992992,"d":550,"ds":"The Ensemble Studio Theatre (EST) is a nonprofit membership-based developmental theatre located in Hell's Kitchen, New York City. It has a dual mission of nurturing individual theatre artists and developing new American plays.","wpu":"Ensemble Studio Theatre","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/EST_New_Logo.png/960px-EST_New_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hell's Kitchen Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":40.762944,"lo":-73.992583,"d":586,"ds":"Hell's Kitchen Park is a 0.58-acre (0.23 ha) park in Hell's Kitchen in Manhattan, New York City.","wpu":"Hell's Kitchen Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Hells_Kitchen_1453.JPG/960px-Hells_Kitchen_1453.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Church of Sts. Cyril & Methodius and St. Raphael","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":40.758889,"lo":-73.996806,"d":704,"ds":"The Catholic Church of Sts. Cyril & Methodius and St. Raphael in Manhattan, New York City has since 1974 been administered as the seat of a Croatian national parish.","wpu":"Church of Sts. Cyril & Methodius and St. Raphael","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Church_of_Sts._Cyril_%26_Methodius_and_St._Raphael_01.jpg/960px-Church_of_Sts._Cyril_%26_Methodius_and_St._Raphael_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Church of the Sacred Heart of Jesus (New York City)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":40.765094,"lo":-73.9904,"d":724,"ds":"The Church of the Sacred Heart of Jesus is a Roman Catholic parish church, located in Hell's Kitchen/Clinton, Manhattan, New York City. Founded in 1876, it is a parish of the Archdiocese of New York and is located at 457 West 51st Street. Sacred Heart of Jesus School is located at 456 West 52nd Street.","wpu":"Church of the Sacred Heart of Jesus (New York City)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Church_of_the_Sacred_Heart_of_Jesus%2C_Manhattan%2C_New_York.jpg/960px-Church_of_the_Sacred_Heart_of_Jesus%2C_Manhattan%2C_New_York.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ars Nova (theater)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":40.76757,"lo":-73.99055,"d":766,"ds":"Ars Nova is an Off-Broadway, non-profit theater in New York City's Hell's Kitchen neighborhood. Ars Nova develops and produces theater, comedy and music created by artists in the early stages of their careers. Besides its Off-off Broadway home in Hell's Kitchen, Ars Nova also operates the former Barrow Street Theatre at Greenwich House as a space for Off-Broadway productions.","wpu":"Ars Nova (theater)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Ars_Nova_%2855283714793%29.jpg/960px-Ars_Nova_%2855283714793%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Westside Theatre","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":40.7595,"lo":-73.9926,"d":815,"ds":"The Westside Theatre is an off-Broadway performance space at 407 West 43rd Street between Ninth and Tenth Avenues in the Hell's Kitchen neighborhood of Manhattan, New York City. The building houses two auditoriums: the Upstairs Theatre, which seats 270, and the Downstairs Theatre, which features a thrust stage and has a seating capacity of 249.","wpu":"Westside Theatre","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/The_Westside_Theatre_%2855282653402%29.jpg/960px-The_Westside_Theatre_%2855282653402%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"The Actors' Temple","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":40.761111,"lo":-73.989167,"d":934,"ds":"The Actors' Temple, officially named Congregation Ezrath Israel, is a non-denominational Jewish synagogue located at 339 West 47th Street, in the Hell's Kitchen neighborhood of Manhattan, New York City, New York, United States.","wpu":"The Actors' Temple","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/The_Actors%27_Temple_%2855283976310%29.jpg/960px-The_Actors%27_Temple_%2855283976310%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"New York, often called New York City (NYC), is the most populous city in the United States. It is located at the southern tip of New York State on New York Harbor, one of the world's largest natural harbors. The city comprises five boroughs—Manhattan, Brooklyn, Queens, the Bronx, and Staten Island—each being coextensive with its respective county.","wpu":"New York City","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/View_of_Empire_State_Building_from_Rockefeller_Center_New_York_City_dllu_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-View_of_Empire_State_Building_from_Rockefeller_Center_New_York_City_dllu_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-26"}